79727841959,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.0064881003178917,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":18.8,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.08444515604757817,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":5.2,"_gate_pool_share":-0.4201577592332405,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.08809550735690208,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":69.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.013510769876535943,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":63.5,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-5.6539249048377355e-05,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.029997570210368973,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":12.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.008593156218242684,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":85.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.11416,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":76.1,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Compass Diversified is a private equity firm specializing in add on acquisitions, buyouts, industry consolidation, recapitalization, late stage, and middle market investments. It seeks to invest in leading industrial or branded consumer companies, textiles, Apparel and Luxury goods, trading companies and distributors, manufacturing, distribution, consumer discretionary, commercial services and supplies, consumer products, capital good, Leisure Product, consumer service, consumer staples, household durables, business services sector, infrastructure healthcare, safety & security, electronic components, food, and foodservice. The firm prefers to invest in companies based in North America. It seeks to invest between $80 million to$800 million and EBITDA starting from $10 million per annum. It seeks to acquire controlling ownership interests in its portfolio companies and can make additional platform acquisitions. The firm prefer to have controlled and majority stake in companies. The firm invests through its balance sheet and typically holds investments between five to seven years. Compass Diversified was incorporated in 1998 and is based in Westport, Connecticut with an additional office in Costa Mesa, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Elias Joseph Sabo | CEO & Director | Age 54","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $460K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["D/B/A Compass Diversified Holdi is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.0B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 35%.","The company is burning through $51M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 11.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 1800% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 8% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.0},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Large open-market insider purchases (net $2.5M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Compass Diversified (CODI) Addresses ADW Capital Concerns, Reports $74.2M Income and Significant Debt Reduction","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/compass-diversified-codi-addresses-adw-capital-concerns-reports-742m-income-and-significant-debt-reduction","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795471618.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here Is Why Bargain Hunters Would Love Fast-paced Mover Compass Diversified Holdi